  areas that we have concerns with  or some areas that we may be receiving  threats for so  an example would be when we had the  theater shootings in colorado  we did a constant omni presence  within those facilities uh for quite  some time and similar to what occurred  with the asian community here recently  um we've had an increase of omnipresence  of officers so the community feels  comfortable  uh that the police department's paying  attention  absolutely you know it's been a full  year now if you can believe it of the  pandemic  are there any new policies within metro  well as you can imagine we were learning  along the way too  um so in the original throws of the  cobid we  it was basically voluntary for the pp  and e and then  subsequently as we saw the positivity  rate increase  we made it mandatory for officers to  wear gloves and masks  and social distancing and washing of the  hands and everything  else that goes along with the pandemic  but then we had to  adjust how we communicated uh with the  public in our public outreach  and in those kind of forums uh what we  do as a police agency with that  community  you know building community trust it's  important that we meet with them on a  regular basis so it that made it very  difficult  in the in the um skype and you know  zoom and microsoft teams world and then  but internally we had to make some  significant cuts associated with it  because of the budget  uh so we had to get rid of some uh  standing units that we've had on an  apartment for quite some time such as  the horse patrol  we've had hiring freezes across the  board we got rid of all our part-time  employees  to the tune of 140 plus individuals  and you know we stopped hiring our or  we had to scale back on the academies  from six to three so we were just hired  for attrition  uh so that that was a big hindrance for  us um  it referenced the cove time period  and now as you can imagine we're going  to try to come out of this  moving forward but 